{
  "id": "TX-HB-1927-2021",
  "scope": "state:tx",
  "title": "H.B. No. 1927, \"Firearm Carry Act of 2021\" (relating to provisions governing the carrying of a firearm by a person who is 21 years of age or older and not otherwise prohibited ...)",
  "urls": [
    "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1927",
    "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/87R/billtext/html/HB01927F.htm",
    "http://journals.house.texas.gov/hjrnl/87r/pdf/87RDAY53FINAL.PDF",
    "http://journals.senate.texas.gov/sjrnl/87r/pdf/87RSJ05-24-F.PDF",
    "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/87R/billtext/pdf/HB01927F.pdf"
  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "Sec. 1: This Act shall be known as the Firearm Carry Act of 2021.\nSec. 22 (amending Penal Code 46.02(a)): (a) A person commits an offense if the person: (1) intentionally, knowingly, or recklessly carries on or about his or her person a handgun; [and] (2) at the time of the offense: (A) is younger than 21 years of age; or (B) has been convicted of an offense under Section 22.01(a)(1), 22.05, 22.07, or 42.01(a)(7) or (8) committed in the five-year period preceding the date the instant offense was committed;\nSec. 22 (46.02(a-5)): (a-5) A person commits an offense if the person carries a handgun and intentionally displays the handgun in plain view of another person in a public place.\nSec. 22 (46.02(a-7)(3)): (3) at the time of the offense, was prohibited from possessing a firearm under Section 46.04(a), (b), or (c).\nSec. 26 (repealer): SECTION 26. The following provisions are repealed: (1) Section 11.041, Alcoholic Beverage Code;\nSec. 26 (repealer, items 8-10): (8) Section 46.02(c), Penal Code; (9) Section 46.03(a-1), Penal Code; and (10) Section 46.035, Penal Code.",
